<title>GERMANY: Weru sees 97 profit, full Caradon takeover.</title>
<headline>Weru sees 97 profit, full Caradon takeover.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Weru AG said on Tuesday it expected 1997 profits to match the previous year and forecast that majority shareholder Caradon Plc would bid for outstanding shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Our goal in 1997 is to achieve operating profits that are comparable with the previous year,&quot; Weru chairman Juergen Bockstette told reporters.</p>
<p>According to preliminary figures, Weru's 1996 operating profit was between 31 and 32 million marks.</p>
<p>Bockstette said the group's largest shareholder -- Britain's Caradon group -- which holds 79.9 percent of Weru shares -- would probably make an offer this year to obtain the remaining shares in the German window and door maker.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, +49 228 26097 150 reuter</p>
</text>
